{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# No forced landing: the primary completion-verify step can be killed mid-run with NO verdict\n\n> **Framing corrected by measurement (see the RCA comment).** This ticket originally said \"a\n> DIFFERENT unproductive cycle now forms\" after bf31. **That is refuted.** An instrumented re-run on\n> `85805e02f1` measured 258 tool calls with **238 distinct signatures (92%)** and **93.8-100% novelty\n> in the FINAL block** — versus bf31's pre-fix 135/264 distinct and **0% novelty** over its last 66\n> calls. bf31's fix worked; the loop is gone. What remains is **genuine, non-repetitive breadth\n> running out of turns**, exactly as [rebar:a89d-4dd2-f421-417a] argued. The defect below is\n> unchanged by that correction, because it holds under either frame.\n\n## The defect\n\nThe primary completion-verify agent step is dispatched with **no forced-landing boundary**, so when\na run's evidence gathering exceeds its budget the run is **killed with no verdict** instead of being\nmade to land with one.\n\n* `build_agent_request` (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/runs.py:327-339`) builds the `RunRequest` for every\n  workflow agent step and never sets `tool_step_limit`. The v3 step schema is closed, so\n  `completion-verification.yaml`'s `decide@then/verify` step has no way to supply one.\n* The shipped forced-landing primitive is therefore dormant for the one step that needs it:\n  `src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py:64-73` rewrites the toolsets to\n  `.filtered(lambda ctx, _: ctx.run_step <= limit)`. Its only production setter is the bounded\n  recovery sub-call (`completion_recovery.py:471`, `_EVIDENCE_TOOL_STEPS=16`).\n* Exceeding the budget raises pydantic-ai `UsageLimitExceeded` -> `interpret_failure`\n  (`structured_run.py:75-101`) raises `LLMRunnerError` -> `CompletionAgentStep.run`\n  (`completion_recovery.py:429-432`) catches only `UnretryableOutputError`, of which `LLMRunnerError`\n  is a strict **ancestor** (`errors.py:29-46`) -> `failure_diagnostic` stays `None` ->\n  `raise_completion_workflow_failure` raises a bare `LLMError` at `completion_recovery.py:400`.\n  No verdict, no `gate_error_v1` sidecar, computed diagnostic discarded one frame from the surface.\n\nConsequence: the only documented exit is `--force-close`, the unattested close this project forbids.\n**20 of 205 epics in this store already carry a `FORCE_CLOSE` audit comment**, including `1d96`\n(21 descendants) and `bf50` (19) — so this is the established escape hatch, not a hypothetical.\n\n## THE LOAD-BEARING REQUIREMENT: there are TWO independent kill paths\n\n`build_usage_limits` (`structured_run.py:399-412`) installs **both**:\n\n    request_limit    = max(1, ceil(eff_max_iter / 2))   # 240 at the default max_iterations=480\n    tool_calls_limit = max(8, eff_max_iter)              # 480\n\n`tool_step_limit` is keyed on `run_ctx.run_step`, which increments once per **model request**\n(`pydantic_ai/_agent_graph.py:856`). It therefore bounds the FIRST path and **does not bound the\nsecond at all**. Measured sweep at the default budget:\n\n| tool calls per request | `tool_step_limit` | outcome |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2 | 239 | OK — verdict returned (478/480 calls) |\n| **3** | 239 | **`LLMRunnerError`** — 483/480 |\n| 3 | 216 (0.9x) | **`LLMRunnerError`** |\n| 3 | 180 (0.75x) | **`LLMRunnerError`** |\n| 6 | 120 (0.5x) | **`LLMRunnerError`** |\n\n**No fraction of `request_limit` can guarantee the landing**, because per-request tool-call fan-out\nis unbounded. My live run sat at 258 calls / 240 requests = **1.075**; [rebar:a89d-4dd2-f421-417a]\nmeasured a real run at **475/240 = 1.979**, clearing the 480 ceiling by **2 calls**. A fix that sets\nonly `tool_step_limit` passes a 1-call-per-request test, looks correct in review, and still dies in\nproduction. That is the trap this ticket must not fall into.\n\nEnforcement point established from the vendored source: `UsageLimits.check_before_tool_call`\n(`pydantic_ai/usage.py:412-419`) is called from `_agent_graph.py:1703-1706` with **projected** usage\n(`usage.tool_calls + len(calls_to_run)`) and raises **before** executing, so `usage.tool_calls`\nnever overshoots the ceiling — the run dies instead. A guard must therefore withdraw tools while\nenough headroom remains for the step it is about to permit.\n\n## The fix\n\n1. **`src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py`** — make the `available` predicate in `build_agent_kwargs`\n   **two-term**. Withdraw tools when EITHER the request allowance is spent OR one more step at the\n   run's own observed tool-call rate would trip `tool_calls_limit`. The second term reads the live\n   `run_ctx.usage.tool_calls`; the reserve is the run's observed calls-per-completed-step (ceil,\n   min 1) — derived and self-calibrating, not a new magic number.\n2. **`src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py`** — expose the ceilings the predicate needs from the SAME\n   place `build_usage_limits` derives them (`:399-412`), so the derivation is single-sourced and\n   cannot drift from the limits actually installed on the call.\n3. **`src/rebar/llm/workflow/runs.py`** — `build_agent_request` sets `tool_step_limit` when the step\n   opts in through a `with:` input. This is the established extension point, stated inline at\n   `runs.py:165-166`: *\"Carried as a `with:` input (not a step field) because the v3 step schema is\n   closed/immutable\"* — precedent `step_budget_per_item`, `output_tokens_per_item`,\n   `output_budget: model_max` (a **sentinel, not a number**), `temperature`.\n4. **`src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/completion-verification.yaml`** — opt the `decide@then/verify`\n   step in.\n\n**Derivation (AC#3), single-sourced off `structured_run.py:407`:** `tool_step_limit =\nmax(0, request_limit - 1)` -> 239 at `max_iterations=480`, 24 at 50, 3 at 8, 0 at 2. Measured:\n`run_step` permits requests `1..limit`, so the landing is request `limit+1` and `limit <=\nrequest_limit - 1`. Do **not** subtract `OUTPUT_RETRIES` — the PROMPTED retry loop calls\n`agent.run_sync` afresh per attempt (`structured_run.py:214-216`) and each attempt gets a fresh\n`run_step` and a fresh request budget (measured: attempt 2 starts at request 8 of a 10-request\nbudget). Use `max(0, ...)` not `max(1, ...)`: at `eff_max_iter=2`, `limit=0` lands in one tool-free\nturn whereas `limit=1` would still exhaust.\n\n## What this does NOT do\n\n**This does not promise a PASS for e369, and must not be described as doing so.** It converts\n\"killed empty, with `--force-close` as the only exit\" into a real `completion_verdict` on the\nevidence actually gathered — i.e. **a verdict on partial evidence**. Two things can still make that\nverdict a FAIL, both out of scope here and tracked separately:\n\n* e369's criterion #1 (\"every child story is closed and its change is `Verified +1` on Gerrit\") has\n  **no evidence any repository tool can reach**, and the deterministic child-closure proof the\n  precheck already computes is collapsed to a boolean at `gate_ops.py:132` and never reaches the\n  verifier's prompt (`completion-verification.yaml` wires only `context`).\n* The step budget is **flat** and does not scale with claim volume — already named in-tree by\n  `99e22e4c23` ([rebar:d59e-e042-2b94-4b70]) and by [rebar:a89d-4dd2-f421-417a].\n\n`completion_verdict` has no INDETERMINATE value (`_norm_verdict` normalizes anything but `\"PASS\"` to\n`\"FAIL\"`), so a forced landing **fails closed** — it blocks a close, never certifies one. An\nunder-evidenced FAIL is already the prompt's sanctioned behaviour\n(`src/rebar/llm/reviewers/completion_verifier.md:150-151`: *\"If, after a bounded search, you cannot\nfind evidence that a requirement is met, record what you searched and treat it as NOT MET — never\nassume.\"*). The residual risk is a *quiet* false FAIL, indistinguishable from a considered one.\n\n## Blast radius\n\n`agent_call.build_agent_kwargs` is on the path of **every** LLM call in the repo (plan-review,\ncode-review, completion). The change is held safe by construction: the new predicate lives **inside**\nthe existing `if req.tool_step_limit is not None and tools:` branch, which no production caller but\nbounded recovery currently enters, and the opt-in is a single `with:` key on ONE workflow step. Every\ncall that does not opt in is byte-identical.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] the primary completion-verify agent step runs with a forced-landing boundary, so tools are\n      withdrawn before the budget is exhausted and the agent must emit a verdict\n- [ ] the boundary bounds **BOTH** kill paths — the `request_limit` path AND the `tool_calls_limit`\n      path — using the live `run_ctx.usage.tool_calls`, not `run_step` alone\n- [ ] a run that would previously have died budget-exhausted instead returns a `completion_verdict`\n      (a test drives a tool-hungry agent and asserts a verdict is produced, not an exception)\n- [ ] the RED test **varies the calls-per-request ratio** and includes a case at ~2+ calls/request\n      that FAILS with a `run_step`-only guard and PASSES with the two-term guard — a fixture pinned\n      at 1 call/request would be vacuous\n- [ ] the limit is derived from the call's own step budget, single-sourced with\n      `build_usage_limits`, rather than a second unrelated magic number\n- [ ] no change to a run that converges normally — a converging run is byte-identical at\n      `tool_step_limit` `None` / 100 / 238 (same request count, same tool surface, same verdict)\n- [ ] `tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_token_recovery.py:132`\n      (`assert runner.requests[-1].tool_step_limit is None`) still passes UNEDITED — it pins the\n      tool-free finalizer, which this change must not touch\n- [ ] the full CI selection (`pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 4 --dist worksteal`)\n      is green apart from the known pre-existing failure [rebar:354d-c85d-6689-4302]\n\n## Testing\n\n    pytest tests/unit/test_agent_call_forced_landing_c827.py -q\n    pytest tests/unit/test_runner_pydantic_budget.py tests/unit/test_agent_call_seam.py \\\n           tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_token_recovery.py -q\n    pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 4 --dist worksteal -q"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785941805904315001,"uuid":"391100f5-db74-4802-be48-b7a3c1c2de8f"}